---This structure contains much of the configuration data for the app monitor.
---@class aws.rum.AppMonitorConfiguration
---@field IdentityPoolId? aws.rum.IdentityPoolId The ID of the Amazon Cognito identity pool that is used to authorize the sending of data to RUM.
---@field ExcludedPages? aws.rum.Pages A list of URLs in your website or application to exclude from RUM data collection.
---@field IncludedPages? aws.rum.Pages If this app monitor is to collect data from only certain pages in your application, this structure lists those pages.
---@field FavoritePages? aws.rum.FavoritePages A list of pages in your application that are to be displayed with a "favorite" icon in the CloudWatch RUM console.
---@field SessionSampleRate? aws.rum.SessionSampleRate Specifies the portion of user sessions to use for RUM data collection. Choosing a higher portion gives you more data but also incurs more costs.
---@field GuestRoleArn? aws.rum.Arn The ARN of the guest IAM role that is attached to the Amazon Cognito identity pool that is used to authorize the sending of data to RUM.
---@field AllowCookies? boolean If you set this to true, the RUM web client sets two cookies, a session cookie and a user cookie. The cookies allow the RUM web client to collect data relating to the number of users an application has and the behavior of the application across a sequence of events. Cookies are stored in the top-level domain of the current page.
---@field Telemetries? aws.rum.Telemetries An array that lists the types of telemetry data that this app monitor is to collect.
---@field EnableXRay? boolean If you set this to true, RUM enables X-Ray tracing for the user sessions that RUM samples. RUM adds an X-Ray trace header to allowed HTTP requests. It also records an X-Ray segment for allowed HTTP requests. You can see traces and segments from these user sessions in the X-Ray console and the CloudWatch ServiceLens console. For more information, see What is X-Ray?

